rrently show state changes with updated badges and arrows; smooth CSS transitions and number-glide animations will be added in **Phase 3 — Add meaningful animations**.\n- **Interactive Prediction (Phase 4)**: The teaching area presents answers step-by-step; optional learner prediction prompts (e.g., \"What will `c` become?\") will be implemented in **Phase 4**.","thinking":"Reviewing the requirements to ensure the output explains operations simply, showing calculations with variable values, conditions with operand/result pairs, and loop/function behavior. This aims for clear, step-by-step explanations of the process as it unfolds.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
